Make libCANdb self-contained: a default logger, header-only spdlog/fmt.

Two things kept the now installed libCANdb (patch 0004) from being usable by
a program of its own:

- The parser logs through kDefaultLogger (log.hpp), which libCANdb declares
  but leaves to the program to define, as a std::shared_ptr to a logger of
  CANdb's bundled spdlog 1.8.5 -- which is not installed, so a program could
  not provide it. Define a default in the library: errors to stderr,
  CDB_LEVEL to change the level (as dbclint does). It is weak, so a
  program's own definition (dbclint's) still takes precedence.
- log.hpp includes spdlog/fmt/ostr.h before spdlog.h, so the bundled fmt 7
  was compiled in its library mode: extern templates (basic_data<void>,
  vformat_to) that nothing in libCANdb defines, and linking a program
  against it failed with undefined fmt::v7 symbols. (dbclint linked only
  because it instantiates them itself.) Build CANdb with the bundled spdlog
  and fmt header-only, as private definitions.

Upstream-Status: Pending


--- a/src/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -3,6 +3,7 @@
   dbcparser.cpp
   parsererror.cpp
   stringutils.cpp
+  default_logger.cpp
 )
 
 file(READ ${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/dbc_grammar.peg DBC_GRAMMAR)
@@ -23,6 +24,11 @@
 target_link_libraries(CANdb PUBLIC cpp-peglib spdlog tl-expected fmt)
 #target_link_libraries(CANdb PUBLIC spdlog fmt)
 target_compile_features(CANdb PUBLIC cxx_std_17)
+# The bundled spdlog and fmt are used header-only, completely inside the
+# library: log.hpp includes spdlog/fmt/ostr.h before spdlog.h, which
+# otherwise left fmt in its compiled-library mode (extern templates nobody
+# defines in a shared libCANdb).
+target_compile_definitions(CANdb PRIVATE SPDLOG_HEADER_ONLY FMT_HEADER_ONLY)
 
 # Install the library and its API headers (dbcparser.h and what it
 # includes) as include/CANdb/.
--- a/src/default_logger.cpp
+++ b/src/default_logger.cpp
@@ -0,0 +1,14 @@
+// The logger CANdb's parser writes to (log.hpp). A program may define its
+// own kDefaultLogger (dbclint does); this one is used otherwise, so that
+// using the library does not require the program to provide a logger.
+// Errors only, on stderr; CDB_LEVEL=debug|info|warn|... changes the level.
+#include "log.hpp"
+#include <cstdlib>
+#include <spdlog/sinks/stdout_sinks.h>
+
+__attribute__((weak)) std::shared_ptr<spdlog::logger> kDefaultLogger = []() {
+    auto logger = std::make_shared<spdlog::logger>("candb", std::make_shared<spdlog::sinks::stderr_sink_mt>());
+    const char* z = std::getenv("CDB_LEVEL");
+    logger->set_level(z ? spdlog::level::from_str(z) : spdlog::level::err);
+    return logger;
+}();
